---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Draft policies"
  description="Draft, not-yet-active policies for the Amalano Glass concept. No sales or application-level data collection are in effect."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="overline">Policies</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:var(--text-2xl);margin:0.6rem 0 1.25rem">
        Draft policies — none in effect yet
      </h1>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          {SITE.name} is a pre-launch concept. There is no store to transact
          with, so there are no active policies. The notes below are drafts that
          describe intent only. They are not offers, terms, or guarantees, and
          they take effect only if and when ordering is switched on.
        </p>

        <p>
          <span class="policy-status">Status: draft — not in effect</span>
        </p>

        <h2>Sales &amp; orders</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this site can be purchased. The cart is a local planning
          tool; there is no checkout, no payment processing, and no way to place
          an order. Any prices shown are placeholder hypotheses, not offers.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy &amp; data</h2>
        <p>
          The Amalano application has no account system, newsletter signup,
          contact form, analytics, advertising, or payment step, so there is no
          personal information to submit to Amalano. The cart is stored only in
          your browser and is not sent by the application. No application or ad
          cookie is set.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hosting provider still processes ordinary web requests. GitHub
          states that GitHub Pages logs and stores visitor IP addresses for
          security purposes; that processing is governed by GitHub's policies.
          See <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages"
          >GitHub Pages data collection</a>. This notice must be replaced with a
          complete data inventory before forms, analytics, support, or checkout
          are added.
        </p>

        <h2>Shipping &amp; fulfillment</h2>
        <p>
          Not established. Because there is no inventory and no order flow, we
          make no claims about shipping methods, timeframes, regions, or costs.
          A real fulfillment policy is one of the things that must exist before
          ordering could open.
        </p>

        <h2>Returns &amp; exchanges</h2>
        <p>
          Not established. With nothing sold, there is nothing to return. A
          written returns-and-exchanges policy would be published alongside a
          real product before any sale.
        </p>

        <h2>Product claims</h2>
        <p>
          We deliberately make no claims about materials, safety, care,
          durability, sustainability, or warranties. Such statements require
          testing and verification we don't yet have. When there is evidence, we
          will say so plainly — and not before.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Support and legal contact details will be published once a registered
          entity stands behind the store. They are intentionally not listed yet,
          because inventing them would be the opposite of the point.
        </p>

        <p>
          For the bigger picture, see the
          <a href={href('/about/')}>about page</a> and the
          <a href={href('/#preview')}>pre-launch note</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
